<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Preveza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1538">1538</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-ottoman-venetian-war">Third Ottoman–Venetian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Preveza was a naval battle fought on 28 September 1538 off Preveza in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, in which the Ottoman fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayreddin-barbarossa">Hayreddin Barbarossa</a> defeated the fleet of the Holy League commanded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrea-doria">Andrea Doria</a>. The victory secured Ottoman naval dominance in the eastern and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> for over three decades, until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lepanto">Battle of Lepanto</a> in 1571.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-preveza.jpg" alt="Battle of Preveza" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osman Nuri Pasha and Hovhannes Umed Behzad (1809–1874) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Preveza_(1538).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…1521, the destruction of the Hungarian royal army at the Battle of Mohács in 1526, the first siege of Vienna in 1529, and the naval operations of Hayreddin Barbarossa, whose victory at <b>Preveza</b> in 1538 secured Ottoman naval dominance in the eastern and central Mediterranean for a generation.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire · Military</a></li></ul></section>
